From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: describe the SOCCP SMP2P and D3 control

Add the SMP2P channel to the SoC Control Processor, using the SMEM
items (617/616), IPCC client (46) and remote PID (19) from the SM8750
vendor devicetree, and a node for the qcom-soccp-sleep driver: the
TCSR word where SOCCP reports its D-state, the SMP2P "sleep" bit (9),
and SOCCP's path to DDR for the vote held while it is awake.

Both are disabled here; boards whose boot firmware leaves SOCCP running
enable them.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -675,6 +675,47 @@
 		/* TODO: smem mailbox in and out */
 	};
 
+	/* SMEM items, IPCC client and PID from the SM8750 vendor devicetree */
+	smp2p_soccp: smp2p-soccp {
+		compatible = "qcom,smp2p";
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&ipcc 46 IPCC_MPROC_SIGNAL_SMP2P
+					     IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+
+		mboxes = <&ipcc 46 IPCC_MPROC_SIGNAL_SMP2P>;
+
+		qcom,smem = <617>, <616>;
+		qcom,local-pid = <0>;
+		qcom,remote-pid = <19>;
+
+		status = "disabled";
+
+		smp2p_soccp_out: master-kernel {
+			qcom,entry-name = "master-kernel";
+			#qcom,smem-state-cells = <1>;
+		};
+
+		smp2p_soccp_in: slave-kernel {
+			qcom,entry-name = "slave-kernel";
+			interrupt-controller;
+			#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+		};
+	};
+
+	/* SOCCP D-state word in TCSR */
+	soccp_sleep: soccp-sleep@1fda000 {
+		compatible = "qcom,sm8750-soccp-sleep";
+		reg = <0x0 0x01fda000 0x0 0x4>;
+
+		qcom,smem-states = <&smp2p_soccp_out 9>;
+		qcom,smem-state-names = "sleep";
+
+		interconnects = <&aggre2_noc MASTER_SOCCP_AGGR_NOC QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS
+				 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>;
+
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+
 	soc: soc@0 {
 		compatible = "simple-bus";
 
